From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:10:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [GDN] recover spec: int16 row-scaled state (FMT=int16_row)

VLLM_GDN_SPEC_STATE=recover now works with --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype int16. The
verify and commit kernels load/store the checkpoint through the int16
row-scale codec (gdn_int16_load_state / gdn_int16_store_state, the same
functions the per-token path uses), dispatched on the constexpr FMT; the
format follows the state dtype and VP = V + scale rows (130 for V=K=128).

With W = 1 the commit re-quantizes once per step from the same fp32 state the
per-token path quantizes into its accepted column, so outputs and the stored
int16 codes/scales are bit-identical to per_token (int16). W > 1 re-quantizes
only on fold (logged; not bit-identical).

Tests: tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_int16.py (4 steps, row and slot
records, align boundary; outputs and int16 state bitwise vs the per-token
Triton path), model-path test int16 variant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
